# Next.js / React UI

## App structure

- App Router only (`src/app`). No Pages Router.
- Use `'use client'` when the file needs state, effects, or browser APIs (see `@src/app/page.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/chatbot.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/header.tsx`).
- Put new UI under `src/app/components/ui/` unless introducing a clearer feature folder by request.
- Backend Route Handlers live under `src/app/api/v1/` (not in the UI tree); keep secrets and LLM/DB work out of client components.

## Styling

- Tailwind + existing shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `ScrollArea`).
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (`@src/lib/utils.ts`).
- Match the dark zinc aesthetic (`bg-zinc-900`, gradients, rounded chat surfaces).
- `components.json` may alias utils to `@/app/lib/utils`; the real file is `@/lib/utils`. Do not duplicate `utils.ts` to “fix” the alias.

## State and exports

- Prefer local `useState` / `useRef` / `useEffect`. Do not add a global store unless justified.
- Match surrounding export style (named for `Chatbot`, hooks, primitives; default where the file already defaults).

## Chat UX invariants

Canonical consumer: `@src/app/components/ui/chatbot.tsx`.

- Render assistant markdown with `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm`
- Stream by appending content chunks to the assistant bubble
- Thread with `parent_id` / server `assistant_message_id`
- Ctrl/Cmd+K clears the thread via `@src/hooks/refreshChatKeyHandler.ts`
- Autoscroll when new messages arrive
- Do not call Telegram (or other side-effect notify APIs) after stream completion

## Resume

- Resume is a static asset at `/resume.pdf` (see header download link). Do not add a custom resume API route unless requested.
